  "id": "COMPOUND:27437 - PROTEIN:6150",
  "verbalization": "Dendridine A appears to interact with H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3 through a series of molecular targets that are all ultimately linked to microtubule-associated protein 1B. This suggests a potential mechanism where Dendridine A modulates the activity of microtubule-associated proteins, which in turn influence the function of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, indicating that Dendridine A may act as a regulator of this transporter through a pathway involving microtubule-associated proteins. The observed relationships highlight a possible role for Dendridine A in modulating ion transport processes, potentially through interactions with microtubule-associated proteins that are central to cellular signaling and transport regulation. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of microtubule-associated proteins in mediating the effects of Dendridine A on the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter.",
